2026-10-09T17:56:10.0868999Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0948729Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0956310Z [0m
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0956823Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0957217Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0957347Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0957829Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0958140Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0958436Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0958575Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0958796Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0958897Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0959138Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0959454Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0959708Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0959988Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0960127Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0960321Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0960541Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0960683Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0960891Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0961133Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0961242Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0961379Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0961688Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0962129Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0968461Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0968626Z I will:
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0968729Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0968875Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0969143Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0969483Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0969842Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0970086Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0970333Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0970648Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0970854Z    /root
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0981455Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T17:56:10.0981880Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1016029Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1016421Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1016575Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1017364Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1017587Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1032739Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1033326Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1041460Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1041977Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1042364Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1042533Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1042690Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1042896Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1043194Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1043595Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1043776Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1043882Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1044133Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1044286Z 
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1044481Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1044750Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-09T17:56:10.1044836Z 
